<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Podolia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Podolia is a historical region in present-day south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moldova">Moldova</a>. It belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Polish crown</a> and became part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> seized it in 1672 but surrendered it under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> in 1699.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/podolia.jpg" alt="Podolia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Богдан Репетило · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A1%D1%82%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B0_%D1%84%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%86%D1%8F.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Large raids, often launched in winter when rivers were frozen, followed steppe routes such as the Muravsky Trail into Muscovy or crossed into <b>Podolia</b> and Volhynia.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crimean-khanate">Crimean Khanate · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>At the same time it expanded eastwards: Algirdas defeated the Golden Horde at the Battle of Blue Waters around 1362, opening the way to Kiev and <b>Podolia</b>, and marched on Moscow three times between 1368 and 1372.</blockquote><a href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Treaty of Karlowitz in 1699, which surrendered most of Hungary and Transylvania to the Habsburgs and <b>Podolia</b> to Poland, and the Treaty of Küçük Kaynarca in 1774, which made the Crimean Khanate independent and gave Russia provisions it later interpreted as a right to protect the sultan’s…</blockquote><a href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Podolia</b>, the steppe and forest land between the Southern Bug and the Dniester, was under the Golden Horde until Algirdas of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania defeated three Tatar princes at the Blue Waters around 1362.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-podolia">Duchy of Podolia</a></li></ul></section>
